From c5813edab92d5d503ba10b651d34f88edb44d618 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:46:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a managed run continues across its owner
 gateway's restart [daveey]

A gateway restart (hermes update) ended every in-flight managed Kanban turn: the owner booked it as a
restart loss, the worker exited 76 and the sweep requeued it reclaimed/owner_restart_lost into a new run
that copied the transcript (133 runs on hermes-hub in 7 days). Now the same run continues.

- Owner (gateway/session_kanban_restart.py): a turn the restart/shutdown Stop ended cleanly is booked as a
  checkpoint: the uncounted owner-restart worker_result gains continuable + a one-time checkpoint token,
  and a restart_checkpoint event (reason core_update_pause) names the stopped admission. A lost child
  (no clean result) keeps today's plain booking.
- Worker (hermes_cli/kanban_worker_client.py): on a terminal receipt whose result is an unconsumed
  checkpoint, it keeps its pid and claim, waits up to CONTINUE_WAIT_S (300 s) for the next owner and asks
  kanban.run for the same attempt again (at most MAX_CONTINUATIONS times). An owner that refuses the
  continuation ends it on the same booking: exit 76, today's uncounted requeue.
- Next owner (gateway/session_kanban_continue.py + session_kanban.kanban_run): on a saved attempt with a
  checkpoint newer than its last admission it proves the continuation safe (same session, stopped
  admission settled interrupted, session readable/non-empty/not rotated, task/run/claim/checkpoint still
  current), answers each tool call the stop left open with "[interrupted by Hermes update at <UTC>:
  re-run if still needed]", records the continuation as the run's newest owner_admitted plus a
  restart_continued event, and submits one continuation admission (<request>#continue:<token>, so a
  retried ask returns the same receipt) to the same session. The managed child runs it with the session
  history and a continuation note as the prompt. Unsafe = kanban_continuation_unsafe, logged and booked
  restart_continue_refused, then the fallback above (next run copies the transcript).
- GATEWAY_RESTART_SAFE stays True; its comment now describes continuation.

Proof
- New tests/gateway/test_kanban_restart_continuation.py (20; 19 exact-anchor mutants of the new conditions all killed). The real probe drives the actual dispatcher
  argv against two gateway.run owners on one scratch home: SIGTERM the first mid-turn, start the second.
  GREEN: same run 1, claim and worker pid through the gap; worker clean_exit 0; task done; runs
  [[1, completed, done]]; events have restart_checkpoint + restart_continued and no reclaimed/crashed/
  owner_restart_lost; one session, admissions [interrupted, completed (#continue:)].
  RED on 0e63306fa5e: checkpointed False, client_exit [owner_restart, 76], events end
  worker_result, worker_result, owner_restart_lost; fake-owner worker test: assert 76 == 0.
- Fallback: owner refusing kanban_continuation_unsafe -> exit 76 -> reclaimed, owner_restart_lost x1,
  consecutive_failures 0 (passes on both, as intended).
- 26 kanban/worker/gateway test files: 1427 passed, 1 skipped.
